      de: ["The Montes de Toledo mountain range separates the major Tagus and Guadiana river basins.", "The highest point is La Villuerca, which stands at an altitude of 1603 meters.", "The geology is defined by Ordovician quartzite ridges, creating an 'Appalachian-style' relief.", "The Cabañeros National Park was officially created within the range in 1995 to protect the Mediterranean ecosystem.", "It represents one of the most critical remaining habitats for the endangered Iberian lynx and the Spanish imperial eagle.", "The range spans a length of approximately 350 kilometers across central Spain."],
